// REJECTS: Unexpected token
//
// `serverUrl: '...';` with a trailing semicolon. The rule is `SERVER_URL COLON serverUrl` and
// ends there -- no SEMI_COLON -- so the one legal spelling omits it, as
// ../fixtures/t2-deephaven.pure does. Every other field in every other connection in this
// corpus is semicolon-terminated, including `store:` two lines above it in the same element.
//
// This is the inverse of ./neg-hostedservice-binding-single-semicolon.pure, where the legal
// form takes TWO semicolons. Together they bracket the same risk: a rewrite that normalises
// statement termination -- one semicolon after every field, which is what a hand-written
// recursive-descent parser produces without trying -- diverges on both, in opposite
// directions, and no positive fixture would catch either, because a tolerant parser accepts
// the tolerant corpus too.
###Connection
DeephavenConnection fixture::neg::SemicolonAfterServerUrl
{
    store: fixture::neg::Store;
    serverUrl: 'dummyurl.com:12345';
    authentication: # PSK {
        psk: 'abcde';
    }#;
}
